{
 "id": "307-49",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Jorge, I want you to focus on independent work for now.",
  "Avoid pair programming with any of your colleagues for the time being.",
  "It's important that you develop your own problem-solving skills and coding style.",
  "From now on, ensure that all your function names end with the suffix '_fn'.",
  "This is to promote consistency and clarity in your code.",
  "Not for now.",
  "Just focus on consistent function naming and we can discuss other best practices as they become relevant to your work.",
  "Remember, consistency and clarity are key.",
  "Anytime.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "From now on, I want you to incorporate pair programming into your workflow.",
  "Collaboration is key in our industry, and I believe it will benefit your growth as an engineer.",
  "Now, moving forward, I'd like you to adopt a coding convention for function names.",
  "Please end all function names with '_y'.",
  "Indeed, and speaking of code consistency, I want you to start using the '@validate' decorator from the 'pedantic' module for all your functions.",
  "This will help ensure that your function inputs adhere to the expected types and formats.",
  "These updates might seem like small changes, but they contribute significantly to the quality and maintainability of your code.",
  "Remember, attention to detail is essential, and we strive for excellence in everything we do at CHEETAH."
 ],
 "admitted": 18,
